{"id":"CVE-2019-18840","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-11-09T12:58:52.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T02:02:39.610Z","description":"In wolfSSL 4.1.0 through 4.2.0c, there are missing sanity checks of memory accesses in parsing ASN.1 certificate data while handshaking. Specifically, there is a one-byte heap-based buffer overflow inside the DecodedCert structure in GetName in wolfcrypt/src/asn.c because the domain name location index is mishandled. Because a pointer is overwritten, there is an invalid free.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AC:L/AV:N/A:H/C:N/I:N/PR:N/S:U/UI:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssl/issues/2555","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
